05 – System Architecture and Technical Design
1. Document Purpose

This document describes the technical architecture and design of the B2B Order Management Platform.

It defines the major system components, their responsibilities, communication methods, data flow, security mechanisms, database design approach, and technology stack.

The purpose of this document is to provide a technical foundation for implementation, testing, maintenance, and future development.

2. System Overview

The B2B Order Management Platform follows a client-server architecture.

The system consists of three primary layers:

Frontend Layer – Provides the user interface and user interaction.
Backend Layer – Provides business logic, REST APIs, authentication, authorization, validation, and error handling.
Database Layer – Stores users, products, inventory, carts, orders, invoices, and audit information.

The general communication flow is:

User → React Frontend → REST API → Express Backend → PostgreSQL Database

The response follows the reverse path:

PostgreSQL Database → Express Backend → REST API → React Frontend → User

