19. Technology Stack

| Layer                     | Technology                             |
| ------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |
| Frontend                  | React                                  |
| Frontend Build Tool       | Vite                                   |
| Backend Runtime           | Node.js                                |
| Backend Framework         | Express.js                             |
| Database                  | PostgreSQL                             |
| Authentication            | JWT                                    |
| API Style                 | REST                                   |
| Version Control           | Git / GitHub                           |
| Development Environment   | Visual Studio Code                     |
| API Testing               | Postman or equivalent API testing tool |
| Optional Containerization | Docker                                 |


20. Deployment Considerations

The project will initially be developed and tested in a local development environment.

The architecture should allow future deployment to a cloud or server environment.

Future deployment may include:

Frontend hosting
Backend hosting
Managed PostgreSQL database
Environment variable configuration
HTTPS
Production logging
Monitoring

Production deployment is outside the initial development scope unless specifically required.

21. Design Principles

The system will follow these principles:

Separation of concerns
Modular development
Reusable components
Secure authentication
Role-based authorization
Input validation
Consistent error handling
Maintainable code structure
Database consistency
Testable functionality
Clear documentation
Reproducible development setup
22. Technical Assumptions

The technical design is based on the following assumptions:

Users have access to a modern web browser.
The backend server can communicate with the PostgreSQL database.
Development environment supports Node.js and npm.
Required environment variables will be configured locally.
Development and testing will use authorized or simulated data.
External production systems will not be accessed without appropriate authorization.
23. Future Technical Enhancements

Potential future technical improvements include:

Docker-based development and deployment
Automated CI/CD pipeline
Cloud deployment
Automated unit and integration testing
API documentation using OpenAPI/Swagger
Advanced monitoring and logging
Redis-based caching
Email notification service
Payment gateway integration
Advanced analytics
24. Conclusion

The proposed architecture provides a structured foundation for developing the B2B Order Management Platform.

The separation of frontend, backend, and database responsibilities improves maintainability and supports future expansion.

React will provide the user interface, Node.js and Express.js will handle business logic and REST APIs, and PostgreSQL will provide persistent relational data storage.

JWT authentication and role-based authorization will protect application resources, while validation, error handling, inventory consistency, and audit activities will support reliable system operation.

